The space $Q$ is a finite oriented Poincaré complex of dimension four. The natural map $f:N\to Q$ has degree one and induces an isomorphism on fundamental groups, identifying both with the group $G$ in <a href="#rf:group" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="rf:group">[rf:group]</a>. If $b$ is the total number of chamber hyperbolic planes in $N$, then $$\pi_2(N)\cong(\mathbb ZG)^{2b}$$ has the specified orthogonal hyperbolic basis, and $\widetilde H_i(\widetilde N;\mathbb Z)=0$ for $i\ne2$. The group $G$ is finitely presented, is torsion-free, and satisfies $$\label{rf:pd}
 H^i(G;\mathbb ZG)=0\quad(i\ne4),\qquad
 H^4(G;\mathbb ZG)\cong\mathbb Z$$ with trivial right $G$-action.

The second Postnikov stages of $N$ and $L$, with the preceding markings, identify over $Q$ with the split stage $$B=EG\times_G K(A,2).$$ There are maps $u_N\colon N\to B$ and $u_L\colon L\to B$ inducing the specified identifications of fundamental and second homotopy groups. If $\Gamma(A)=H_4(K(A,2);\mathbb Z)$, then $$\label{st:homology-extension}
 0\longrightarrow\Gamma(A)_G\longrightarrow H_4(B;\mathbb Z)
 \longrightarrow H_4(Q;\mathbb Z)\longrightarrow0$$ is a split exact sequence.

For every $R\geq 0$ there is a constant $c_Z(R)<\infty$ such that $$\|T\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq\|T\|_{\max}
 \leq c_Z(R)\|T\|_{\mathrm{op}}
 \qquad(T\in\mathbb C[Z],\ \mathop{\mathrm{prop}}(T)\leq R).$$ Consequently, operator-norm convergence of algebraic Roe operators with one common propagation bound implies convergence in maximal norm.

Every bounded finite-propagation operator $D$ on $H_Z$ acts by left and right multiplication on $\mathbb C[Z]$, and these actions extend to a multiplier of $A_Z$. This assignment is a faithful $*$-homomorphism and satisfies $$\|D\|_{\mathrm{op}}\leq \|D\|_{M(A_Z)}
 \leq c_Z(R)\|D\|_{\mathrm{op}}
 \qquad\text{if }\mathop{\mathrm{prop}}(D)\leq R.$$ For an operator supported on a single matching, the multiplier norm equals the concrete norm.
